  "body": "I'm hoping to write a tool to update firmware on a device using WebUSB but part of the process requires writing data to a mass storage interface on the same device. (normally I would use dd) I am confused as to whether this is currently possible or or not using WebUSB.\r\n\r\nFor instance:\r\n\r\n- Issue #64 regarding access to mass storage states: \"WebUSB is the right solution if you are working with a device that doesn't implement a standard device class.\" Clearly this is not quite true since WebUSB is used for HID and other kinds of devices that implement class compliant interfaces.\r\n- Over on [StackOverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/49162692/can-webusb-transfer-files-to-a-usb-mass-storage-device-or-act-like-dd): \"It cannot. USB mass storage devices are claimed by the system's generic USB mass storage class driver and are therefore unavailable to the browser.\"\r\n- Yet Issue #164 discusses accessing various kinds of USB mass storage drives via WebUSB. This would suggest that it IS actually possible.\r\n\r\nCan someone help to clarify the situation? Obviously if the OS is USING a specific device it wouldn't be available, but I am hoping in the case of MSD that if the device is ejected from the host OS that it would be possible to use it directly from WebUSB.\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n",
